{"name":"Abra Cadabra","hex":"#966165","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abra-cadabra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of abracadabra."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abra-cadabra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abra Cadabra","blocks":[{"text":"Aaron Philips, known professionally as Abra Cadabra, is a British rapper and singer. He is a member of the UK drill group OFB."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abra_Cadabra"},{"title":"Abra Cadabra (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Abra Cadabra is a 1983 Australian animated fantasy musical comedy film written, co-produced and directed by Alexander Stitt, The film is inspired on the tale of the Pied Piper of Hamelin. Starring John Farnham and Jacki Weaver, it is the first ever animated feature film to be filmed in stereoscopic 3-D."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5c/Abra_Cadabra_VHS_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abra_Cadabra_(film)"},{"title":"Theora mesopotamica","blocks":[{"text":"Theora mesopotamica is a species of saltwater and brackish water clam, a bivalve mollusk in the family Semelidae. This species is known from the northwestern end of the Persian Gulf, and from subfossil remains in brackish deposits in the lower Tigris–Euphrates basin of Iraq."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Corbula_mesopotamica_right_valve.jpg/330px-Corbula_mesopotamica_right_valve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theora_mesopotamica"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Corbula_mesopotamica_left_valve.jpg/500px-Corbula_mesopotamica_left_valve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Corbula_mesopotamica_left_va